# Byte-exactness rules for this repository.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching line wins, so the general rule comes first and
# the byte-exact exception comes last.
#
# Text is stored and checked out as LF on every platform. Without this, a Windows
# clone (core.autocrlf=true) would materialize CRLF in the working copy, and the
# tests that read src/ files as text — and the build's own output — would then
# differ between machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored tree is hashed (tools/vendor-skills.ts, vendor/PROVENANCE.json) and
# listed file-by-file with its sha256 in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, where
# tools/verify-notices.mjs --check fails if those bytes change.
# vendor/whalechan-image-character/references/reference-catalog.json carries CRLF,
# written that way by the upstream Python tool that produced it, and the recorded
# digest covers exactly those bytes. So this subtree is declared "never touch my
# bytes": no normalization on commit, no conversion on checkout, on any platform.
vendor/** -text -eol
